<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41981" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rūgo</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i> [1. ruga]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to crease</i>, <i>wrinkle;</i> transf., of the dress (cf. 1. ruga,
			B.), <i>to become wrinkled</i> or <i>rumpled</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vide palliolum ut rugat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 2, 3, 30</span></i>
			: pallium, id. Fragm. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 18,
				12, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to wrinkle</i> any
			thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frontem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 50, 2</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to corrugate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">testae (concharum) rugatae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 33, 52, § 102</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
